<aside class="notes">
r is literally the two "Before"/"After" diagrams from a few slides
back, written as one complex number: its size *r* is how clustered
the phases are, its angle psi is the shared rhythm they've locked
onto. The schematic above makes both pieces of the equation visible
at once: each theta_j is one dot's angle on the unit circle, and
r e^(i psi) -- the orange arrow -- is their average as a single
complex number, with its own length r and angle psi.
</aside>

---

### Dynamical systems & bifurcation

Below a critical coupling strength, synchrony never happens.\
Above it, it suddenly does.\
That sudden flip has a name: a bifurcation.

