<aside class="notes">
Order parameter r at steady state, as a function of coupling K, for
the same spread-0.7 noisy frequency distribution as the Sync Dial's
default (averaged over several random draws -- the shaded band shows
how much that steady-state r varies from one random draw to another).
Flat and low, then a sudden climb around K_c: that's the bifurcation.
Point back at the Sync Dial slide -- this is the curve the room was
tracing out live by dragging K.
</aside>

---

### Network science

Real synchronising systems -- power grids, neurons, cardiac tissue,
the fireflies -- aren't tidy pairs. They're networks. Whether they
sync at all depends on the properties of the network.

